   "name": "Antichrist Dihedral",
   "grade": "5.10c",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": null,
   "description": null,
   "approach": "Follow the High Sierra Trail to Tamarack Lake, where most parties camp; a day trip from Lone Pine Meadow is also possible. From the lake it is about an hour up to the Main Wall, a north-facing wall above the Lilliput Glacier. The route aims for the huge dihedral on the left flank of the tooth at mid-wall, reached by crack and ledge climbing into a left-facing corner.",
   "descent_text": "From the top-out, scramble fourth class west into the gap that separates the main wall from Dawn Pillar and rappel into it (slung block and a single-bolt anchor), then scramble out the far side and hike third class down to a prominent gully. Another rappel drops into the gully, and from there you scramble down; take gear to build or back up anchors. The main wall can also be descended by going over the summit and east then north to Lion Rock Pass (class 2) and back to the lake.",
